      "chunk_003"
    ],
    "reason": "The text in chunk_003 explicitly states that training compares the model's predicted token probabilities with the next tokens in the training examples. It further explains that a loss function measures this prediction error and backpropagation computes gradients used by an optimizer to update model parameters, directly answering how parameters are adjusted."
  },
  "question_0002": {
    "answered": true,
    "evidence_ids": [
      "chunk_001",
      "chunk_003"
    ],
    "reason": "Chunk_001 mentions that a validation dataset supports model selection and choice of training settings. Chunk_003 clarifies the specific mechanism: 'Early stopping uses validation performance to decide when to end training, rather than selecting a stopping point using the held-out test results.' This confirms the utilization of validation data for determining the end of training."
  },
  "question_0003": {
    "answered": false,
    "evidence_ids": [
      "chunk_001",
      "chunk_005"
    ],
    "reason": "The text mentions that a held-out test dataset measures performance (chunk_001) and that evaluation must distinguish retrieval quality from generated answer quality (chunk_005). However, the specific metrics or criteria defining 'performance' for the held-out test set are not explicitly listed as a single definition; chunk_005 implies they involve factual correctness and support but does not provide a comprehensive list of all criteria used specifically by the test dataset in contrast to others."
  },
  "question_0004": {
    "answered": false,
    "evidence_ids": [
      "chunk_001"
    ],
    "reason": "Chunk_001 states that 'Dataset size alone does not establish dataset quality' but does not specify what other characteristics constitute quality. No other passage provides a list of factors defining dataset quality."
  },
  "question_0005": {
    "answered": false,
    "evidence_ids": [
      "chunk_001"
    ],
    "reason": "Chunk_001 states that if passages from the same source appear in both training and testing, measured performance can overstate ability. However, it does not explain the underlying mechanism (e.g., memorization vs. generalization) or why this specifically leads to an overstatement."
  },
  "question_0006": {
    "answered": false,
    "evidence_ids": [
      "chunk_002"
    ],
    "reason": "Chunk_002 states that a causal attention mask prevents a position from attending to later positions. It does not explain the technical mechanism (e.g., setting weights to zero or negative infinity) by which this restriction is enforced."
  },
  "question_0007": {
    "answered": false,
    "evidence_ids": [
      "chunk_002"
    ],
    "reason": "Chunk_002 describes the function of the causal attention mask but does not state what specific consequence occurs for the model's output if the mask were removed or applied incorrectly."
  },
  "question_0008": {
    "answered": false,
    "evidence_ids": [
      "chunk_002"
    ],
    "reason": "Chunk_002 mentions that a finite context window limits the amount of text available. It does not explain specifically how this limit restricts the model's ability to connect information across a passage (e.g., by cutting off attention weights beyond a certain distance)."
  },
  "question_0009": {
    "answered": false,
    "evidence_ids": [
      "chunk_002",
      "chunk_005"
    ],
    "reason": "Chunk_002 states that an attention weight does not establish that a claim is true. Chunk_005 adds that an answer can cite a passage while making unsupported claims. However, the text does not explain the specific reason why attention weights fail to establish truth (e.g., hallucination, distractors) nor explicitly defines an alternative metric required for verification beyond general 'factual correctness'."
  },
  "question_0010": {
    "answered": false,
    "evidence_ids": [
      "chunk_001",
      "chunk_003"
    ],
    "reason": "Chunk_001 mentions validation supports model selection. Chunk_003 states early stopping uses validation performance to end training. While this implies a role in distinguishing generalization, the text does not explicitly explain the mechanism of how validation data distinguishes generalization from overfitting or its functional difference from test results beyond 'not using held-out test results' for stopping."
  },
  "question_0011": {
    "answered": false,
    "evidence_ids": [
      "chunk_003"
    ],
    "reason": "Chunk_003 defines dropout as randomly disabling activations during training and notes ordinary inference uses the trained network without that. It does not explain the specific characteristics of this 'random disabling' regarding learning dynamics or the mathematical/architectural implications (e.g., preventing co-adaptation)."
  },
  "question_0012": {
    "answered": false,
    "evidence_ids": [
      "chunk_003"
    ],
    "reason": "Chunk_003 defines overfitting as improved training performance failing to translate to unseen examples. It does not explain the specific characteristics of data or model capacity leading to this scenario, nor how dataset quality influences it."
  },
  "question_0013": {
    "answered": false,
    "evidence_ids": [
      "chunk_004"
    ],
    "reason": "Chunk_004 states that a retrieval encoder maps questions and passages into embeddings. It does not explain the specific mathematical transformation or process used to convert text inputs into these vector representations."
  },
  "question_0014": {
    "answered": false,
    "evidence_ids": [
      "chunk_004"
    ],
    "reason": "Chunk_004 mentions that a similarity search selects candidate passages. It does not specify the metric or distance function (e.g., cosine similarity) used in this search."
  },
  "question_0015": {
    "answered": false,
    "evidence_ids": [
      "chunk_004"
    ],
    "reason": "Chunk_004 states that selected passages are added to the language model's context. It does not explain the specific method or architectural constraint (e.g., truncation, concatenation) used to integrate these passages into the context window."
  },
  "question_0016": {
    "answered": false,
    "evidence_ids": [
      "chunk_005"
    ],
    "reason": "Chunk_005 defines retrieval recall and precision. It states that neither measure alone shows correct usage and that a highly ranked passage can be irrelevant. However, it does not explain how the system specifically distinguishes between high recall and high precision in operation or defines the differentiation mechanism."
  }
}
